When tourists think of Los Angeles, many think of Hollywood, celebrities, and Disneyland. Locals think of heavy _traffic_.

There are nearly 8 million [cars registered in Los Angeles County](https://www.laalmanac.com/transport/tr02.php). There is no place for defective vehicles on the packed freeways and bustling city streets.

But what happens if you end up buying a vehicle with manufacturer defects?

Fortunately, you’re _not_ out of luck - thanks to lemon law in Los Angeles.

Assuming the vehicle is covered under warranty, the manufacturer is obligated to repair any defects. If they are unsuccessful in doing so, you may be eligible for a lemon law claim. Recognizing a lemon and understanding your rights under the California lemon law are crucial steps toward a favorable resolution.

We created this guide to empower Los Angeles residents with knowledge and tools to properly address their defective vehicles.

