## Steps to Take If You Have a Lemon

As a consumer, your role in a [Los Angeles lemon law claim](/blog/tips-for-lemon-law-challenges-in-los-angeles) is not extensive or complicated, but it’s extremely important.

## 1. Know Your Warranty Terms

For starters, you need to understand the specifics of your vehicle’s warranty, as it forms the basis of your lemon law claim. This primarily includes the duration or mileage. For instance, Chevrolet provides new car warranties valid for 3 years or 36,000 miles. Your warranty needs to be valid when you first report the defect to the manufacturer.

Keep in mind, California lemon law applies to used vehicles in addition to new ones. If the vehicle is sold with a dealer warranty - and meets the terms of the state’s lemon laws - you may file a claim.

## 2. Keep Detailed Records

All lemon law cases are based on the documents you provide. Most importantly, you’ll need to keep and organize records of every repair attempt, including dates, descriptions of the problem, and the dealer’s response.

Additionally, a lemon law buyback should include all incidental costs. This would include towing fees, hotel stays, car/Lyft/Uber costs, and so on. When you meet with a lemon law lawyer in Los Angeles, they will advise you on all the documentation to prepare.

## 3. Consult a Lemon Law Expert in Los Angeles

Once you have documentation to prove you have a lemon, the next step is meeting with a lawyer with experience in Los Angeles lemon law. Most offer free consultations to determine the validity of your claim.

The lemon lawyer will evaluate your case and advise on the best course of action.

## 4. Your Consumer Rights Under Lemon Law in California

If you win a California lemon law claim, you may request the following compensation:

- Vehicle replacement with a new, identical model or one of equal value.

- A buyback of the defective vehicle, including reimbursement for the down payment, monthly payments, and any payoff of the loan balance.

- Recovery of costs and attorney fees.

- Recovery of all incidental costs associated with the lemon.

Lemon law attorneys work to hold vehicle manufacturers accountable for everything listed above.

